## New exact discriminator

For the four lateral exits, the Block28 joint matrix is

\[
 Q_\lambda=\frac{1-\lambda}{16}J_4+\frac{\lambda}{4}I_4,
 \qquad
 \operatorname{spec}Q_\lambda=
 \left\{\frac14,\frac\lambda4,\frac\lambda4,\frac\lambda4\right\}.
\]

Therefore

\[
 \operatorname{rank}_+(Q_0)=1,
 \qquad
 \operatorname{rank}_+(Q_{1/2})=4.
\]

The lower bound is ordinary matrix rank and the upper bound is the matrix
dimension.  Thus `lambda=0` is the product of two uniform one-tip laws, while
every separable left/right realization of `lambda=1/2` needs at least a
four-valued shared cause.

One abstract four-state realization is explicit.  Let `Z` be uniform on the
four exits and put

\[
 A(g\mid Z=z)=2^{-1/2}\delta_{gz}
 +\frac{1-2^{-1/2}}4.
\]

Then

\[
 q_{1/2}(g,h)=\frac14\sum_z A(g\mid z)A(h\mid z).
\]

This does not yet supply a physical Record carrier, causal preparation,
transport, debit, or renewal for `Z`.  It identifies the next missing physics
more precisely than “find more CP/TP channels.”

For front `f`, the pair moment is

\[
 \mathbb E_\lambda[g^ih^j]
 =\frac{\lambda}{2}(\delta^{ij}-f^if^j).
\]

All one-tip marginals, additive Record counts, Blank debits, and observables
of the form `A(g)+B(h)` are independent of `lambda`.  Hence an additive
single-tip Record current or source cannot see this fork.  Only a pair
correlator can distinguish it, and identifying that correlator with a
stress-energy source would require a separate bridge theorem.

